 3. ⚠️ FBI hack raises data alarms 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The FBI is facing its second hack in three months — and this breach could affect local law enforcement and anyone who has been arrested or reported missing, Axios cybersecurity reporter Sam Sabin writes. 

 President Trump told Fox News yesterday that the hack is "not good," but said "maybe we'll learn things that we would have never learned otherwise" — including about what he describes as the "Russia hoax." 🔎 Zoom in : The FBI is investigating an apparent breach of its National Crime Information Center, which shares information among local and national law enforcement agencies, CNN and NBC reported Friday night. 

 The NCIC connects data between local and national law enforcement about criminal subjects, suspected terrorists, missing persons (including children) and similar information, Cynthia Kaiser, a former top FBI cyber official, tells Axios. Zoom out: Several news outlets say the U.S. Department of Agriculture is dealing with a breach of its system that facilitates farmer payments.

 The NSA and FAA have also faced tech outages amid a broader wave of disruptions this month. Keep reading . 

 
 
