 4. 📱 Global crackdown on kids&#x27; social media 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Axios research. Chart: Axios Visuals Australia created a blueprint last December, becoming the first country to ban social media for kids under 16, Axios' Sara Fischer writes in an Axios Media Trends Executive briefing. 

 Now others, including the U.K. and France, are considering following suit. What to watch: In the U.S., kids' online safety regulation has faced an uphill climb in Congress.

 Cities and states have proposed their own measures, like age verification provisions, school cellphone bans and time limits . Read on ... Subscribe to Axios Media Trends Executive . 

 
 
