 5. 🔎 Dems target ICE&#x27;s pricey prison purchases 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The Trump administration's $3.3 billion spending spree on immigrant detention facilities is about to face an intense new wave of scrutiny.

 Why it matters: Democrats have spent two years furiously writing letters over allegations of ICE and DHS corruption. Starting in January, those letters can turn into subpoenas, Axios' Brittany Gibson writes. Zoom in: As of mid-November, ICE has paid $230 million to $739 million apiece for six detention facilities from CoreCivic and The GEO Group, two private prison companies that have secured major government contracts and reported record revenue since President Trump's return to office.

 ICE often paid double the warehouses' assessed value, GAO found . Keep reading . 

 
 
