 6. 🦠 1 map to go: Measles surge 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: CDC . Map: Brad Jennings/Axios U.S. measles cases have climbed past 5,800 so far this year — more than 20 times the total just two years ago — as the nation lost its measles-elimination status for the first time since 2000.

 Pennsylvania leads the nation by far with 1,605 cases, followed by South Carolina (670), Wisconsin (657) and Utah (536). Share this map . 

 
 
